POW.SYSTEMS =E2=80=94 Priority One: Get the Data Flowing

Decision
<p>Do not build infrastructure for its own sake.</p>
<p>Do not start with Docker.<br>
Do not start with Prefect.<br>
Do not start with Grafana.<br>
Do not start with Kafka.<br>
Do not start with a lakehouse.<br>
Do not start with a dashboard.</p>
<p><strong>Priority one is simple: begin preserving irreversible data immed=
iately.</strong></p>
<p>The first version should be almost embarrassingly simple:</p>
<p>SOURCE<br>
=E2=86=92 Python collector<br>
=E2=86=92 validation<br>
=E2=86=92 compressed raw file<br>
=E2=86=92 R2<br>
=E2=86=92 tiny run ledger<br>
=E2=86=92 repeat forever</p>
<p>Everything else can be rebuilt later from the raw history.</p>
<p>Missing history cannot.</p>



1. Use one VPS you already pay for
<p>Pick one existing VPS and dedicate it to POW collection.</p>
<p>Name it:</p>
<p>pow-garden-01</p>
<p>It needs:</p>
<ul>
<li>Linux</li>
<li>Python 3</li>
<li>git</li>
<li>uv or venv/pip</li>
<li>cron or systemd timers</li>
<li>sqlite initially</li>
<li>rclone or boto3/S3 client for R2</li>
<li>curl</li>
<li>jq</li>
<li>optionally DuckDB/Polars for transformations later</li>
</ul>
<p>That is enough.</p>
<p>No containers required.</p>



2. Minimal repo
<p>Create one repo:</p>
<p>pow/</p>
<p>Structure:</p>
<p>pow/<br>
