<p>Do not build a giant framework.</p>
<p>Every source should only need:</p>
<ol>
<li>fetch</li>
<li>validate</li>
<li>save raw</li>
<li>record run</li>
</ol>



3. R2 is the permanent memory
<p>Create:</p>
<p>pow-raw</p>
<p>Optionally later:</p>
<p>pow-lake<br>
pow-private<br>
pow-artifacts</p>
<p>But only pow-raw matters on Day 1.</p>
<p>Use paths like:</p>
<p>raw/<br>
domain=3Dparts/<br>
source=3Dmouser/<br>
year=3D2026/<br>
month=3D09/<br>
day=3D20/<br>
hour=3D23/<br>
2026-09-20T23-15-00Z.jsonl.gz</p>
<p>Every successful fetch gets pushed to R2 immediately.</p>
<p>Local disk is scratch only.</p>
<p>If the VPS dies, replace it.</p>
<p>If R2 history survives, the garden survives.</p>



4. Every collector writes a manifest
<p>Example source.yaml:</p>
<p>id: parts.mouser<br>
domain: parts</p>
<p>schedule: =E2=80=9C*/15 * * * *=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>primary:<br>
type: api</p>
<p>fallback:<br>
type: none</p>
<p>freshness_slo_minutes: 30</p>
<p>irreversibility: 5</p>
<p>retention:<br>
raw_allowed: true<br>
derived_allowed: true</p>
<p>identity:<br>
primary_key: manufacturer_part_number</p>
<p>why_preserve:</p>
<ul>
<li>live inventory</li>
<li>live lead time</li>
<li>price state</li>
<li>lifecycle changes</li>
</ul>
<p>target_transformations:</p>
<ul>
<li>component_scarcity</li>
<li>repair_feasibility</li>
<li>repair_margin</li>
</ul>
<p>Do not collect data without knowing why it matters.</p>



5. Every run records one row
<p>Use SQLite first.</p>
<p>Table:</p>
<p>collection_runs</p>
<p>Fields:</p>
<p>run_id<br>
source_id<br>
scheduled_for<br>
started_at<br>
completed_at<br>
status<br>
route_used<br>
records_seen<br>
records_changed<br>
raw_bytes<br>
payload_hash<br>
schema_hash<br>
r2_uri<br>
error<br>
collector_version</p>
<p>That is enough to answer:</p>
<ul>
<li>did it run?</li>
<li>when?</li>
<li>what did it collect?</li>
<li>did data change?</li>
<li>where is the raw file?</li>
<li>did schema change?</li>
<li>did it fail?</li>
</ul>
<p>No dashboard required yet.</p>



6. Use systemd timers or cron
<p>For V1, use systemd timers if convenient because they are easy to inspec=
t and restart.</p>
<p>Example collector command:</p>
<p>python -m kernel.run parts.mouser</p>
<p>or:</p>
<p>./scripts/run-source parts.mouser</p>
<p>Schedules can be generated from the source manifests later.</p>
<p>Do not waste time building a scheduler initially.</p>
<p>The target is:</p>
<p>Mouser every 15m<br>
DigiKey every 15m<br>
Fuel Finder every 30m<br>
Apprenticeships every 30=E2=80=9360m<br>
NESO around publication cadence<br>
compute/mining existing cadence<br>
EV feeds as frequently as practical</p>
<p>Get the first irreversible sources running.</p>
<p>Then consolidate scheduling later.</p>



7. Collector flow
<p>Every collector should do exactly:</p>
<ol>
<li>fetch</li>
<li>confirm HTTP/API success</li>
<li>basic schema check</li>
<li>timestamp observation</li>
<li>hash payload</li>
<li>compress</li>
<li>upload to R2</li>
<li>verify upload</li>
<li>record collection_runs row</li>
<li>exit 0</li>
</ol>
<p>If anything fails:</p>
<ul>
<li>record failed run</li>
<li>retry</li>
<li>alert if freshness SLO will be violated</li>
</ul>
<p>Do NOT make normalization a prerequisite for preserving raw.</p>
<p>The raw response must survive even if downstream code is broken.</p>



8. Fallbacks later, not before primary collection works
<p>Do not spend hours designing fallback ladders before one source even col=
lects.</p>
<p>First:</p>
<p>primary source<br>
=E2=86=92 reliable collection<br>
=E2=86=92 R2 history</p>
<p>Then add fallback for important sources.</p>
<p>When a fallback exists, store:</p>
<p>route_used =3D primary<br>
or<br>
route_used =3D fallback_csv<br>
or<br>
route_used =3D fallback_api</p>
<p>Never silently mix sources.</p>



9. Very basic health monitoring
<p>Create:</p>
<p>pow-health.py</p>
<p>It reads the source manifests + collection_runs and asks:</p>
<p>For each source:</p>
<p>now - last_valid_run &gt; freshness_slo?</p>
<p>If yes:</p>
<p>STALE</p>
<p>If no valid run within 2=C3=97 SLO:</p>
<p>GAP_FORMING</p>
<p>Output:</p>
<p>Mouser          HEALTHY   8m<br>
DigiKey         HEALTHY   11m<br>
Fuel Finder     HEALTHY   21m<br>
Apprentices     STALE     79m<br>
EV Gridserve    GAP       14m</p>
<p>This is enough initially.</p>
<p>Run it every five minutes.</p>
<p>Send alert by email/webhook if a source enters:</p>
<p>GAP_FORMING<br>
FAILED<br>
SCHEMA_CHANGED</p>



10. External dead-man switch
<p>Because the VPS can die completely, have one independent check outside i=
t.</p>
<p>Simplest options:</p>
<ul>
<li>Healthchecks.io</li>
<li>Better Stack</li>
<li>a tiny Cloudflare scheduled Worker</li>
</ul>
<p>The VPS pings every 5 minutes.</p>
<p>If no heartbeat for 10=E2=80=9315 minutes:</p>
<p>alert.</p>
<p>That is the only external monitoring required for V1.</p>



